      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Thank you for splitting out the DFU status helpers and updating the commit message. There are a few edge-case/cleanup bugs in `dfu_download` and missing unit test coverage to address before approval.\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality:** ❌ A few edge cases and cleanup paths need attention in `RtsUsbDevice::dfu_download`:\n- Guard against empty `firmware` and `transfer_size_ \u003d\u003d 0` (which would cause `while (offset \u003c total_size)` to loop infinitely).\n- Reset `dfu_interface_ \u003d -1` if `libusb_claim_interface()` fails so `release()` does not later call `libusb_release_interface()` on an unclaimed interface, and release the claimed interface on the early error returns inside the download loop.\n- Check `ret !\u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(chunk_size)` on `libusb_control_transfer()` so short writes are caught rather than advancing `offset` and corrupting the flashed image.\n**Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** ❌ `util/rts5817_flash.cc` is not yet compiled in `util/build.mk` and couples the DFU protocol chunking loop directly to `libusb_*` calls. Sibling C++ USB flashers in `util/` (`util/elan/`, `util/focaltech/`, `util/egis/`) separate USB transport operations behind a small virtual interface/seam so the protocol state machine can be unit-tested in `utils-test`.\n**Code Simplicity:** ❌ Using `size_t` for `printed_pct` and `pct` avoids the double cast (`uint64_t` -\u003e `size_t`) in the progress calculation.\n**Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** ❌ Extract the magic progress step `10` into a named `constexpr` constant (`kDfuProgressStepPct`), and consider taking `std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e` for `firmware`.\n**Security:** ✅ No security vulnerabilities identified.\n**Testing:** ❌ Automated unit tests are required for `dfu_download` (covering chunking boundaries `\u003c transfer_size_`, `\u003d\u003d transfer_size_`, `transfer_size_ + 1`, final ZLP, and transfer/poll failure paths) via a small virtual seam or mock USB backend, as noted in the inline comment.\n**CL Size \u0026 Scope:** ✅ `Size: M (+135, -4)`. Well-scoped to implementing `dfu_download` after splitting the status helpers into the parent CL.\n**Commit Message:** ✅ Clear, concise high-level summary of the motivation and change.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/18748e91-0dc2-4d16-beb6-33599aa4af20)",
