      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Functionality \u0026 Edge Cases:** There are three precondition and state-cleanup issues in the setup phase of `dfu_download`:\n\n1. **Empty `firmware` payload:** If `firmware.empty()` is true, `while (offset \u003c total_size)` is skipped and `dfu_download` immediately sends a zero-length `DFU_DOWNLOAD` packet and triggers the manifest phase.\n2. **Zero `transfer_size_` infinite loop:** `find_dfu_interface()` parses `transfer_size_` directly from the USB descriptor (`sz[0] | (sz[1] \u003c\u003c 8)`). If a malformed descriptor reports `wTransferSize \u003d\u003d 0`, `chunk_size` evaluates to `0` and `while (offset \u003c total_size)` loops infinitely without advancing `offset`.\n3. **Unclaimed `dfu_interface_` state on `libusb_claim_interface` failure:** `find_dfu_interface()` sets `dfu_interface_ \u003e\u003d 0`. If `libusb_claim_interface()` fails at line 498, `dfu_interface_` remains `\u003e\u003d 0`, causing `release()` (called in `~RtsUsbDevice()`) to call `libusb_release_interface()` on an interface that was never claimed.\n\nConsider also accepting `std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e` (`#include \u003cspan\u003e`) instead of `const std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e \u0026` so callers can pass any contiguous byte buffer:\n\n```cpp\nbool RtsUsbDevice::dfu_download(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e firmware)\n{\n\tif (!dev_handle_ || firmware.empty())\n\t\treturn false;\n\n\t/* Step 1: Find the DFU interface. */\n\tif (!find_dfu_interface() || transfer_size_ \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\tdfu_interface_ \u003d -1;\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n\n\t/* Detach the kernel driver from the DFU interface, if any. */\n\tif (libusb_kernel_driver_active(dev_handle_, dfu_interface_) \u003d\u003d 1) {\n\t\tint kd_ret \u003d libusb_detach_kernel_driver(dev_handle_,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t dfu_interface_);\n\t\tif (kd_ret \u003c 0) {\n\t\t\tfprintf(stderr,\n\t\t\t\t\"Warning: cannot detach kernel driver: %s\\n\",\n\t\t\t\tlibusb_error_name(kd_ret));\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tint ret \u003d libusb_claim_interface(dev_handle_, dfu_interface_);\n\tif (ret \u003c 0) {\n\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"Error: cannot claim DFU interface: %s\\n\",\n\t\t\tlibusb_error_name(ret));\n\t\tdfu_interface_ \u003d -1;\n\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/18748e91-0dc2-4d16-beb6-33599aa4af20)",
