      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **No Magic Values \u0026 Code Simplicity:** Please extract the progress step threshold `10` into a named constant (e.g., `kDfuProgressStepPct`), and use `size_t` for `printed_pct` and `pct` (matching `offset` and `total_size`) to avoid casting `offset` to `uint64_t` and then casting `pct` back to `size_t` for `printf(\"%zu%%\", ...)`:\n\n```cpp\n\t\t/* Print progress every 10%. */\n\t\tconstexpr size_t kDfuProgressStepPct \u003d 10;\n\t\tsize_t pct \u003d offset * 100 / total_size;\n\t\tif (pct \u003e\u003d printed_pct + kDfuProgressStepPct) {\n\t\t\tprintf(\"\\r  Progress: %zu%%\", pct);\n\t\t\tfflush(stdout);\n\t\t\tprinted_pct \u003d pct;\n\t\t}\n```\n(With `size_t printed_pct \u003d 0;` at line 509.)\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/18748e91-0dc2-4d16-beb6-33599aa4af20)",
