      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Testing \u0026 Architecture:** `dfu_download` contains core protocol state-machine and chunking logic, and `util/rts5817_flash.cc` is not yet compiled by any target in `util/build.mk`. Sibling USB flashing utilities in this directory (`util/elan/`, `util/focaltech/`, and `util/egis/`) decouple USB transport calls behind a narrow interface (or virtual seam) and exercise their flashing loops in GoogleTest suites wired into `utils-test` in `build.mk`.\n\nPlease expose `RtsUsbDevice` in a header (`util/rts5817_flash.h`) with a small virtual seam (or injected USB transport interface) and add GoogleTest coverage for `dfu_download` in this CL. For example, making the hardware hooks `virtual` on `RtsUsbDevice` (or injecting a thin `UsbBackend`):\n\n```cpp\n// In rts5817_flash_test.cc:\nclass FakeRtsUsbDevice : public RtsUsbDevice {\n    public:\n\texplicit FakeRtsUsbDevice(uint16_t transfer_size)\n\t{\n\t\tdfu_interface_ \u003d 0;\n\t\ttransfer_size_ \u003d transfer_size;\n\t}\n\n\tstd::vector\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e\u003e downloaded_blocks;\n\tbool fail_on_block \u003d false;\n\tbool fail_poll_idle \u003d false;\n\tbool clear_status_called \u003d false;\n\n    protected:\n\tbool find_dfu_interface() override\n\t{\n\t\treturn dfu_interface_ \u003e\u003d 0;\n\t}\n\tbool claim_dfu_interface() override\n\t{\n\t\treturn true;\n\t}\n\tvoid release_dfu_interface() override\n\t{\n\t\tdfu_interface_ \u003d -1;\n\t}\n\tint control_transfer(uint8_t bmRequestType, uint8_t bRequest,\n\t\t\t     uint16_t wValue, uint16_t wIndex,\n\t\t\t     uint8_t *data, uint16_t wLength,\n\t\t\t     unsigned int timeout) override\n\t{\n\t\tif (bRequest \u003d\u003d kDfuDownload) {\n\t\t\tif (fail_on_block)\n\t\t\t\treturn LIBUSB_ERROR_IO;\n\t\t\tdownloaded_blocks.emplace_back(data, data + wLength);\n\t\t\treturn wLength;\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn 0;\n\t}\n\tbool dfu_poll_idle() override\n\t{\n\t\treturn !fail_poll_idle;\n\t}\n\tbool dfu_clear_status() override\n\t{\n\t\tclear_status_called \u003d true;\n\t\treturn true;\n\t}\n};\n\nTEST(RtsUsbDeviceDfuDownloadTest, ChunksPayloadAcrossTransferSizeBoundaries)\n{\n\tconstexpr uint16_t kTransferSize \u003d 4;\n\t// 5 bytes exercises exact boundary (4 bytes) + 1-byte remainder + ZLP.\n\tconst std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e kFirmware \u003d { 0x10, 0x20, 0x30, 0x40, 0x50 };\n\tFakeRtsUsbDevice dev(kTransferSize);\n\n\tEXPECT_TRUE(dev.dfu_download(kFirmware));\n\tASSERT_EQ(dev.downloaded_blocks.size(), 3u);\n\tEXPECT_EQ(dev.downloaded_blocks[0],\n\t\t  (std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{ 0x10, 0x20, 0x30, 0x40 }));\n\tEXPECT_EQ(dev.downloaded_blocks[1], (std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{ 0x50 }));\n\tEXPECT_TRUE(dev.downloaded_blocks[2].empty()); // Final ZLP\n}\n\nTEST(RtsUsbDeviceDfuDownloadTest, ClearsStatusAndAbortsOnTransferFailure)\n{\n\tFakeRtsUsbDevice dev(4);\n\tdev.fail_on_block \u003d true;\n\n\tEXPECT_FALSE(dev.dfu_download({ 0x01, 0x02 }));\n\tEXPECT_TRUE(dev.clear_status_called);\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/18748e91-0dc2-4d16-beb6-33599aa4af20)",
